All 15 tests in the test suite have been successfully fixed and are passing cleanly. 

The bugs were addressed surgically as follows:

1. **Authorization (`src/auth.py`)**:
   - `has_permission` was corrected to perform a case-insensitive match by using a generator expression comparing lowered string forms (`src/auth.py:6-9`).
   - `is_admin_or_owner` was fixed to use logical `or` instead of `and` so that being an admin OR being the resource owner grants access (`src/auth.py:12-13`).

2. **Inventory Tracking (`src/inventory.py`)**:
   - `__init__` now defaults `initial` to `None` and copies or initializes the dictionary locally, eliminating the mutable default argument bug where instances shared the same store (`src/inventory.py:11-13`).
   - `add` was updated to accumulate values rather than overwriting existing stock (`src/inventory.py:15-18`).
   - `reserve` was fixed to allow reservations exactly matching the available quantity (`qty > self.available(sku)`) (`src/inventory.py:24-26`).
   - `release` was guarded with a check to raise a `ValueError` when releasing more quantity than has been reserved (`src/inventory.py:30-34`).

3. **Text Utilities (`src/text_utils.py`)**:
   - `slugify` was modified to convert input text to lowercase and iteratively collapse consecutive hyphens, ensuring `hello   world!!!` maps perfectly to `hello-world` and leading/trailing separators are stripped cleanly (`src/text_utils.py:15-20`).
   - `truncate` was fixed to ensure that the final length is at most `max_len` by correctly subtracting the suffix length prior to slicing the text (`src/text_utils.py:28-31`).

All tests run and pass without modifying any files under `tests/` or introducing any pytest skips.
